.TH PMCAPTURE 1 "June 2026" "RAFT System Controller" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmcapture \- RAFT INA power data capture daemon and control CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmcapture
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B daemon
[\fB\-\-debug\fR|\fB-d\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B start
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B arm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B disarm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B stop
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B status
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B pmcapture
.B ping
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmcapture
controls the System Controller (SC) INA power sampling service built on
RAFT board JSON and sensor drivers. A long-lived supervisor
(\fBpmcapture.service\fR) runs in the idle state after boot and does
not touch I2C until a capture session is started.
.PP
Use \fBstart\fR to poll configured INA rails and write samples to a local
file (offline SSH analysis) or stream JSON lines over TCP (BEAM PM
Dashboard). Use \fBstop\fR to end a session early. Only one session may run
at a time.
.PP
Use \fBarm\fR to enter GPIO-triggered file capture: the daemon watches a
board trigger line (libgpiod v2 edge events) and starts a capture session
on assert and stops it on deassert. While armed, manual \fBstart\fR is
rejected. Use \fBdisarm\fR to release the trigger line and return to idle.
No I2C traffic occurs until a GPIO-gated capture window is active.
.PP
Board sensor layout is read from RAFT
.I xserver/raft_services/power_management/board/<BOARD>.json
(selected from \fB/bin/sc-board-id\fR when available, otherwise FRU EEPROM product
name — same logic as raft-startup, including revision-specific JSON such as
\fIVEK386-A1.json\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the idle supervisor in the foreground. Intended for
\fBpmcapture.service\fR; listens on the Unix control socket and
maintains \fIstatus.json\fR.
.TP
.B start
Begin a capture session. Exits after sending the request; sampling runs
inside the daemon. When \fB\-\-duration\fR is non-zero, the session stops
automatically after that many seconds. Not allowed while the daemon is
\fBarmed\fR for GPIO capture.
.TP
.B arm
Load a capture profile and/or GPIO trigger options, resolve the GPIO line
name to a chip/offset, and start edge monitoring. Requires \fB\-\-gpio\fR
or a capture config with a \fBtrigger\fR block. Daemon state becomes
\fBarmed\fR. Each GPIO assert→deassert window writes a separate file under
\fI/data/pmcapture/\fR with an auto-generated \fIgpioN\fR suffix. Requires
\fIpython3-gpiod\fR (libgpiod v2) on the System Controller image.
.TP
.B disarm
Stop the trigger monitor. If a GPIO-gated session is running, stop it
first. Returns the daemon to \fBidle\fR.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the active capture session. When \fBarmed\fR, returns to \fBarmed\fR
(not idle) so further GPIO windows may run until \fBdisarm\fR.
.TP
.B status
Report daemon state (\fBidle\fR, \fBarmed\fR, \fBrunning\fR, or \fBerror\fR), a
\fBcapture:\fR summary line distinguishing armed monitoring from active I2C
sampling, optional trigger metadata (\fIgpio\fR, \fItrigger condition\fR,
\fIwindows_completed\fR), and active session metadata (rails, output path,
elapsed time, sample count, \fIrequested_rate_hz\fR and \fIactual_rate_hz\fR
on one line while sampling). Use \fB-j\fR, \fB--json\fR for machine-readable output
(includes \fIsampling_active\fR, \fIarmed\fR, and \fIcapture.phase\fR).
.TP
.B ping
Verify the daemon responds on the control socket.
.SH START OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-rails " " \fISELECTOR\fR, \fB-r " " \fISELECTOR\fR
Which rails to sample from board JSON \fBPOWER SENSORS\fR before optional
capture-config trim. Default \fIall\fR: every power sensor on the board.
Alternatively pass a \fBPOWER DOMAIN\fR \fIName\fR (same as
\fBraft-pm-cmd listdomain\fR, e.g. \fBLPD\fR, \fBAIE\fR), or a
comma-separated list of rail names (e.g.
\fBVCCINT_1,VCC_AIE_1\fR). Legacy values \fIpower_sensors\fR and
\fIpower_domains\fR are treated as \fIall\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-config " " \fIPATH\fR, \fB-c " " \fIPATH\fR
Optional user JSON file that may set \fIrails\fR (selector string or ordered
array of rail names), \fIrate_hz\fR, \fIduration_s\fR, \fIoutput\fR,
\fIoutput_file\fR, and \fIfile_format\fR. \fIPATH\fR may be relative to the
shell working directory or use \fB~\fR. CLI flags override unset config fields.
.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fIMODE\fR, \fB-o " " \fIMODE\fR
\fIfile\fR (default): write capture log on the SC filesystem.
\fItcp\fR: stream newline-delimited JSON on \fB\-\-port\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-rate " " \fIHZ\fR, \fB-t " " \fIHZ\fR
Target sample rate in Hz (0.1–50, default 20).
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fISECONDS\fR, \fB-d " " \fISECONDS\fR
Capture length in seconds. \fI0\fR (default): run until \fBstop\fR or
daemon shutdown.
.TP
.BR \-\-output-file " " \fIPATH\fR, \fB-f " " \fIPATH\fR
Output path for file mode. When omitted, a name is generated under
\fI/data/pmcapture/\fR as
.IR capture_<board>_<timestamp>.<ext>
(or
.IR capture_<board>_<timestamp>_gpioN.<ext>
for GPIO windows).
The directory is created on first file capture when \fI/data\fR is available.
.TP
.BR \-\-file-format " " \fIFMT\fR, \fB-F " " \fIFMT\fR
\fIjsonl\fR (default) or \fIcsv\fR (columnar, one row per sample).
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " \fIADDR\fR, \fB-H " " \fIADDR\fR
TCP bind address for \fB\-\-output tcp\fR (default \fI0.0.0.0\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fINUM\fR, \fB-p " " \fINUM\fR
TCP port for \fB\-\-output tcp\fR (default 18094).
.TP
.BR \-\-client " " \fINAME\fR, \fB-u " " \fINAME\fR
Session owner label recorded in status (default stored value \fIcli\fR;
\fBpmcapture status\fR displays \fBCLI\fR, \fBBEAM\fR, or \fBGPIO\fR for known
clients). BEAM TCP sessions use \fIbeam\fR; GPIO windows use \fIgpio\fR.
.SH ARM OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-gpio " " \fINAME\fR, \fB-g " " \fINAME\fR
Logical GPIO name. Required unless the capture config includes a
\fBtrigger\fR block. Overrides \fBtrigger.gpio\fR when both are given.
.TP
.BR \-\-trigger-active " " \fIhigh\fR|\fIlow\fR, \fB-a " " \fIhigh\fR|\fIlow\fR
Active level that opens a capture window (default \fIhigh\fR). Overrides
the JSON \fBtrigger.active\fR field when both are given.
.TP
.BR \-\-debounce-ms " " \fIMS\fR, \fB-b " " \fIMS\fR
Debounce interval in milliseconds before accepting GPIO edges (default
.IR 0 ).
Overrides the JSON \fBtrigger.debounce_ms\fR field when both are given.
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-config " " \fIPATH\fR, \fB-c " " \fIPATH\fR
Optional user JSON file containing sampling options and/or a \fBtrigger\fR
object (see \fBTRIGGER CONFIG JSON\fR). \fIPATH\fR may be relative to the
shell working directory or use \fB~\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-rails " " \fISELECTOR\fR, \fB-r " " \fISELECTOR\fR
Rail selector (same semantics as \fBstart\fR; default
.IR all ).
.TP
.BR \-\-rate " " \fIHZ\fR, \fB-t " " \fIHZ\fR
Target sample rate in Hz for triggered windows (0.1–50, default 20).
.TP
.BR \-\-file-format " " \fIFMT\fR, \fB-F " " \fIFMT\fR
Output format for triggered file capture (default \fIjsonl\fR). GPIO
triggered capture supports \fIfile\fR mode only.
.TP
.BR \-\-output-file " " \fIPATH\fR, \fB-f " " \fIPATH\fR
Optional fixed output path. When omitted, each GPIO window gets a
separate auto-generated name under \fI/data/pmcapture/\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/pmcapture
CLI entry (symlink into RAFT install tree).
.TP
.I /usr/share/raft/examples/python/pmcapture/
Program modules.
.TP
.I /run/pmcapture/control.sock
Daemon control socket (JSON request/response, one line per message).
.TP
.I /run/pmcapture/status.json
Daemon and session state (\fIidle\fR, \fIarmed\fR, \fIrunning\fR, or
\fIerror\fR; optional \fItrigger\fR and session metadata).
.TP
.I /data/pmcapture/
Default directory for auto-generated capture logs (created on first file
capture; requires \fI/data\fR to be mounted).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/pmcapture.service
systemd unit (\fBExecStart=.../pmcapture daemon\fR).
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.SS jsonl
First line is a catalog object (\fBtype\fR=\fIcatalog\fR) describing
rails and domains. Each following line is one sample object with
\fBts\fR, \fBrails\fR (name → \fBV\fR/\fBI\fR/\fBW\fR), \fBboard\fR, and
\fBrate\fR. Inspect capture files with standard tools such as \fBless\fR or
\fBjq\fR after copy off the SC.
.SS csv
Header row:
\fBts,rate_hz\fR plus \fI<RAIL>_V\fR, \fI<RAIL>_I\fR, \fI<RAIL>_W\fR for each
active rail; one data row per sample. No catalog line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS CAPTURE CONFIG JSON
A JSON file for \fB\-\-capture-config\fR (\fB\-c\fR) may set \fIrails\fR,
\fIrate_hz\fR, \fIduration_s\fR, \fIoutput\fR, \fIoutput_file\fR, and
\fIfile_format\fR. \fIrails\fR is either a selector string (same as
\fB\-\-rails\fR) or an ordered array of rail names. Deprecated
\fIrails_pool\fR / \fIrails_selection\fR are accepted as selector aliases.
CLI flags override any unset field.
.PP
\fBRail subset (CSV, 60 s)\fR
.RS
.nf
{
  "rails": [
    "VCCINT_1",
    "VCCINT_2",
    "VCC_AIE_1",
    "VCC_AIE_2"
  ],
  "rate_hz": 20,
  "duration_s": 60,
  "output": "file",
  "file_format": "csv"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBAll sensors (JSONL, until stop)\fR
.RS
.nf
{
  "rails": "all",
  "rate_hz": 20,
  "duration_s": 0,
  "output": "file",
  "file_format": "jsonl"
}
.fi
.RE
.SS TRIGGER CONFIG JSON
For \fBarm\fR, supply \fB\-\-gpio\fR on the command line or include a
\fBtrigger\fR object in the capture config JSON. CLI trigger flags override
the JSON \fBtrigger\fR block when both are given.
GPIO names are resolved via libgpiod utilities (\fBgpioinfo\fR) or
\fBline_offset_from_id\fR on .IR /dev/gpiochip* .
.PP
\fBGPIO-gated file capture (standard DUT→SC trigger line, CSV)\fR
.RS
.nf
{
  "rails": ["VCCINT", "VCCAIE"],
  "rate_hz": 20,
  "output": "file",
  "file_format": "csv",
  "trigger": {
    "gpio": "SYSCTRL_GPI4",
    "active": "high",
    "debounce_ms": 0
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Board-specific device-tree labels (for example legacy readback names) also
resolve when present in \fBgpioinfo\fR or via libgpiod on \fI/dev/gpiochip*\fR.
.PP
Optional \fBtrigger.chip\fR and \fBtrigger.line\fR override automatic name
resolution. \fBtrigger.active\fR is \fIhigh\fR (default) or \fIlow\fR.
.SS Example commands
Timed file capture to a specific path (120 s, LPD domain rails, CSV):
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pmcapture start \\
  \-\-duration 120 \\
  \-\-output-file /data/pmcapture.out \\
  \-\-file-format csv \\
  \-\-rails LPD
.fi
.RE
.PP
Capture VCCINT and VCC_AIE rails only (comma-separated names):
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pmcapture start \\
  \-\-rails VCCINT_1,VCCINT_2,VCCINT_3,VCCINT_4,VCC_AIE_1,VCC_AIE_2,VCC_AIE_3,VCC_AIE_4 \\
  \-\-duration 60 \\
  \-\-file-format csv
.fi
.RE
.PP
File capture with user rail subset from a JSON file (see
\fBCAPTURE CONFIG JSON\fR above; auto-named capture file under
\fI/data/pmcapture/\fR when no \fB\-\-output-file\fR is set):
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pmcapture start \\
  \-\-duration 60 \\
  \-\-capture-config /data/pmcapture/subset.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Arm GPIO-triggered capture from CLI flags:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pmcapture arm \\
  \-\-gpio SYSCTRL_GPI4 \\
  \-\-rails all \\
  \-\-file-format csv
pmcapture status
sudo pmcapture disarm
.fi
.RE
.PP
Arm from a JSON profile and inspect status:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pmcapture arm \\
  \-\-capture-config /etc/pmcapture/trigger_capture.json
pmcapture status
sudo pmcapture disarm
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check daemon and session status:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pmcapture ping
pmcapture status
pmcapture status --json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop an open-ended capture:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pmcapture stop
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed (daemon unreachable, capture already running, invalid
config, sensor init failure, etc.). Failure messages are printed on
stderr with an \fBERROR:\fR prefix.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage (stderr message uses an \fBERROR:\fR prefix).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (\fBdaemon\fR foreground mode).
